course: dictionary
lesson: 3932
title: Feelings in words: frustration
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Frustration is a cross, upset feeling. You feel it when you cannot do something or cannot get what you want. «Frustration is the hot, stuck feeling when something will not work.» The word stuck is a clue: the feeling is about being blocked.
explain: Read the rest of the sentence for more clues. «A short break, a fresh look and asking for help usually beat giving up.» So when frustration comes, a break and a fresh look can help you keep going instead of quitting.
explain: The word can also mean a thing that causes the feeling. In «play that always ends in frustration», frustration is what the play leads to. Swap in your meaning: "play that always ends in a cross, upset feeling" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Frustration means a cross, upset feeling when you cannot do something or get what you want.
fact: «Frustration» can also mean a thing that causes this feeling.
fact: Useful phrases: «in frustration», «feel frustration», and «a source of frustration».
fact: «Venting» means letting out frustration, as in «That shout is a way of letting out frustration, called venting.»
fact: Calm ways to deal with frustration are to take a deep breath, take a break, ask for help, and try again.
exercise: «Frustration is the hot, stuck feeling when something will not work.» What is frustration? | A kind of deep sleep | A long walk in the rain | A happy feeling when a game goes well | *A cross, upset feeling when you cannot do something
exercise: Mia has been stuck on a hard puzzle for an hour. Which is a calm way to deal with her frustration? | *Take a deep breath and ask for help | Give up and never try again | Shout at everyone in the house | Throw the puzzle across the room
exercise: «That shout is a way of letting out frustration.» What is letting out frustration called? | Sleeping | Counting | Whispering | *Venting
test: «In play, let a pet catch the toy sometimes; play that always ends in frustration makes animals stressed or snappy.» Why should you let a pet catch the toy sometimes? | *So the pet does not get stressed or snappy | So the pet gets bored and sleeps | So the toy will break quickly | So the pet learns to bark
test: «The broken printer was a source of frustration for the whole class.» What does «a source of frustration» mean? | A happy surprise for everyone | *Something that causes a cross, upset feeling | A place where water comes from | A kind of quiet game
exam: «A short break, a fresh look and asking for help usually beat giving up.» What is a good first step when you feel frustration? | Shout until someone comes to you | Throw your work in the bin | Give up straight away | *Take a short break and ask for help
